{
  "reason": "Tier 2: replace symmetric cosine compatibility with a jointly trained asymmetric bilinear scorer. The trajectory shows that more negatives, recency features, residual connections, and auxiliary supervision have not surpassed 0.5737; the latest trial reached 0.5500. A remaining representational limitation is that tied cosine scoring constrains directional item compatibility, motivating a scoring-component change while retaining shared embeddings, whose separation previously hurt performance.",
  "module": [
    "model_design",
    "training_evaluation"
  ],
  "plan": {
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": null,
    "model_design": "Modify GRURec.score to apply a learned asymmetric transformation to features before comparing them with the existing normalized candidate embeddings. Implement transformed_features = features + (features @ self.compatibility_u) @ self.compatibility_v.T / sqrt(16), using dim-by-16 parameters, random initialization for compatibility_u, and zero initialization for compatibility_v; normalize transformed_features before the existing scaled dot product and item bias. This initially reproduces the cosine scorer while allowing directional compatibility without introducing separate item tables or independently fitted scores. Preserve GRURec.__init__, encode, score, predict, existing variable names, and all current representation and loss components so this scorer replacement is the sole experimental change.",
    "training_evaluation": "Update write_predict_script and checkpoint checks to reconstruct and strictly load compatibility_u and compatibility_v within exactly one newly trained model per category, preserving train_category and predictor signatures. Verify initial scoring equivalence, finite gradients for the new parameters, and prediction parity after reload; allow compatibility_u to have zero gradients initially because compatibility_v starts at zero. Keep the current losses, sampling, optimizer, seeds, epoch default 200, checkpoint selection, validation protocol, and identical validation/inference preprocessing unchanged; preserve all four routes, DATA_DIR=os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], trial-local artifacts, and single-GPU execution. Compare measured pinned-host macro HR@10 against 0.5500 and 0.5737 within the shared budget, leave hidden-test inference to the host, and print the measured local score using print(f'Final Validation Score: {score}')."
  }
}
